DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ttccggeettwwiinnssiizzee() function gets the terminal window size of the terminal
     of which _f_d is an open file descriptor and stores it in the _w_i_n_s_i_z_e
     structure of which _w is a pointer.

     The ttccsseettwwiinnssiizzee() function sets the terminal window size of the terminal
     of which _f_d is an open file descriptor from the _w_i_n_s_i_z_e structure refer‐
     enced by _w.  The change occurs immediately.  If the terminal window size
     of the terminal is changed successfully to have a value that is different
     from the value that it had before the ttccsseettwwiinnssiizzee() call, then the
     SIGWINCH signal is sent to all those members of the foreground process
     group of the terminal that have the terminal as their controlling termi‐
     nal.

     The above declaration of _s_t_r_u_c_t _w_i_n_s_i_z_e may not be literal.  It is pro‐
     vided only to list the accessible members.  Therefore, before calling
     ttccsseettwwiinnssiizzee(), the members of the _w_i_n_s_i_z_e structure must be initialized
     by calling ttccggeettwwiinnssiizzee().  The information in a _w_i_n_s_i_z_e structure is
     stored by the kernel in order to provide a consistent interface, but it
     is not used by the kernel.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
     The ttccggeettwwiinnssiizzee() and ttccsseettwwiinnssiizzee() functions return the value 0 if
     successful; otherwise the value -1 is returned and the global variable
     _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the error.  The terminal window size remains un‐
     changed if ttccsseettwwiinnssiizzee() fails.

